// Copy this directory to a kebab-case slug and add metadata.json.
// A Project must cover: purpose/assumptions/non-goals, workflows, requirements,
// NFR decisions, roles, domain relationships, focused tables and indexes,
// transactions/retention, resource APIs, relevant events, 5+ failures,
// consistency/concurrency, caching/jobs, 5+ security controls, observability,
// unit/integration/contract/E2E/concurrency/failure tests, deployment,
// 1K/100K/1M+ workload scenarios, and three readable Mermaid diagrams.
//
// Scale: call `scale({ start, middle, large })` from `./helpers`; each stage is
// [architecture, decision rule] written for this domain. Content tests reject
// sentences shared by three or more projects.
// Diagrams: `diagrams(context, architecture, sequence)` takes flowchart edges and
// sequence messages. Do not put ";" inside a sequence message; Mermaid treats it
// as a statement separator.
// Import `Project` from `@/lib/types` and register the completed content in
// `content/projects/index.ts`, then run `npm run og` to generate its Open Graph
// image and `npm run validate` before opening a PR.
